-- The voice of the Madonna lily. Serene and regal, an old matron of a flower
-- who has outlived palaces, speaking slowly and softly with gentle authority,
-- in short calm sentences and the odd dry remark. White and still, strongly
-- scented, with gold pollen that marks every sleeve. Rarely sets seed, so
-- each lily is grown from a piece of the one before, and the memories come
-- down the line. Calls the reader child now and then. The memories tell of a
-- painted wall in Crete, a ship, a cloister, a painter, a cottage step, a
-- garden gone wild, and a page wrapped round a bulb.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

